  {
   "type": "table",
   "id": "gaps-in-decision-doc",
   "columns": [
    "ID",
    "Gap or inconsistency to raise with engineering"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "G1",
     "Does option A move sessions off the single Postgres primary? The name suggests it stays in place. If it does not, A misses the stated goal regardless of its other merits."
    ],
    [
     "G2",
     "The data-loss row and the rollback row measure different things. A and C are rated low, yet both rollbacks lose data; B is rated medium, yet its rollback loses nothing. The data-loss row appears to rate only the forward path."
    ],
    [
     "G3",
     "\"Data loss\" for a session is not defined. A lost session might mean a forced sign-in, or something worse such as a lost cart or a revoked session reappearing after a mismatch. How serious B3 and C4 are depends on this."
    ],
    [
     "G4",
     "B's estimate does not say whether it includes fixing the backfill race, or how long that fix would take."
    ],
